#NEXUS

[ curryrogers2001a_fig4: Slanted cladogram on a spine (classed slanted): under the out-of-scope ruling for slanted cladograms on a spine (otero2010a_fig15), flagged. Alamosaurus and Titanosaurus both leave the Saltasaurinae node, a polytomy of three. Decimal support values and the node letters A-C (black dots) are not encoded; the clade names printed beside the spine are kept. 17 tips, 1 polytomies (3 children); 4 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 10 case (census 3, seed 20261274). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

